      "problem": "An office chair is marked down by $15%$ during a promotion. What is the sale price of the chair if its original price is $$85?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find an amount that's $15%$ *less than* $$85,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%-15%=85%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n85%=\\frac{85}{100}=0.85\n$$\n\nSo, to find $85%$ of $$85,$ we multiply $$85$ by $0.85:$\n\n$$\n0.85\\cdot $85=$72.25\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sale price of the chair is $$72.25.$",
